      "pins": ["U22.1", "U22.2", "U22.4", "U26.1", "U26.2", "U26.4"],
      "nets": ["/NET0098", "NET0015", "NET0046", "Net-(U17-Y)"],
      "observed": "The buffer symbols have an active-low enable (/OE) and a push-pull output, while their component value says SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, an open-drain buffer without an enable. The listed MPN is U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R, a different tri-state push-pull buffer. For example, U22 has /OE on pin 1, input A on pin 2, and output Y on pin 4; U26's output Y is connected to U22's /OE.",
      "expected": "The specification describes the e-stop circuit as SN74LVC1G07 buffers used as /OE-controlled sinks. The selected component identity and output behavior should match that intended sink function; the stated SN74LVC1G07 part does not provide /OE, and the listed 1G125 MPN is not an open-drain sink.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an e-stop loop ... gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U22\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"1\") (name \"/OE\") (type \"input\")) (pin (num \"2\") (name \"A\") (type \"input\")) (pin (num \"4\") (name \"Y\") (type \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U22\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"/OE\")) (node (ref \"U26\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The e-stop sink path may not have the intended open-drain behavior. A push-pull output can actively drive the shared e-stop line high rather than only sinking it, potentially preventing a safe e-stop assertion or causing contention with another sink.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The buffer value, symbol pinout, and sourcing MPN identify incompatible device behaviors. This mismatch is particularly consequential in the e-stop path, which the specification says relies on enabled sink outputs."
}

